# Prettier 3.9.6 never converges on this file, so `format:check` could not pass
# whatever we wrote. Characterised: a task-list item (`- [ ] ` or `- [x] `)
# whose content starts at column 6 and which carries a wrapped continuation
# paragraph gets that paragraph's continuation lines re-indented from 6 to 10,
# then to 14, and so on, four spaces per run. A plain `- ` item is stable, and
# so is a single-line continuation; it needs both the checkbox offset and the
# wrap. TODO.md has such paragraphs under both checked and open items
# (measured 2026-09-11).
#
# Flattening them into one line each would satisfy the formatter and make the
# durable checklist worse to read, so the file is excluded until the bug is
# fixed upstream. Re-check on the next prettier upgrade and delete this if it
# has gone.
